# ResinCompute - ignore rules.
#
# Ported in spirit from Sibling-C's .gitignore, trimmed to what this tree
# actually produces. Rule of thumb inherited from that sibling: anything the runtime
# MUTATES, anything re-fetchable, and anything holding a credential stays out
# of history. Authored source and hand-written fixtures stay in.

# --- Secrets. NEVER commit. ---------------------------------------------
# The Enka client needs no key, but a local override file is the obvious place
# a token would land, so it is pre-ignored rather than added after the leak.
secrets.json
secrets.local.json
config/secrets.json
api-key*.txt
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Runtime state (mutates constantly) ---------------------------------
# ops/runtime/ holds health.json, pid files and the restart trigger. It is
# written atomically by the supervisor and is never source.
#
# Ignore the CONTENTS, not the directory, and re-admit the .gitkeep. A bare
# `ops/runtime/` also swallows the marker file, so the directory does not exist
# in a fresh clone and the first atomic write fails on a missing parent - the
# supervisor's very first heartbeat. The negation is why the pattern needs the
# trailing `*` rather than the directory form: git will not re-include a file
# whose parent directory is itself excluded.
ops/runtime/*
!ops/runtime/.gitkeep
restart_trigger.txt

# --- Logs ---------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
*.log.[0-9]

# --- Fetched payload cache ----------------------------------------------
# Enka / Project Amber responses are cached here honouring the response ttl.
# Re-fetchable by definition, and it is third-party game data we deliberately
# do not vendor (SPEC_SCAFFOLD section 4). data/fixtures/ IS tracked - those
# are hand-authored minimal test fixtures.
data/cache/
data/*.tmp
# The account snapshot is RUNTIME state written by headless/jobs.py persist_state
# and read by surface/. It carries a player UID and a roster, it changes on every
# pass, and it is a display cache rather than source - see core/state_io.py.
data/account_state.json

# --- Python bytecode + tool caches --------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Virtualenvs --------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Local-only tooling config (may carry server URLs or tokens) --------
# The blanket ignore stays: settings.local.json and the session/cache junk under
# .claude/ are per-machine and can carry server URLs or tokens.
#
# THE COMMAND DOCS ARE THE EXCEPTION, and it is not a preference. A ritual that
# is not version controlled does not reach a fresh clone, is not scanned by
# docs-guards.yml, and cannot be reviewed in a diff - the same shape of failure
# as core.hooksPath, where the tracked directory is useless if nothing points at
# it. Sibling-C ran with 11 command docs under zero version control and its
# drift guard names that as one of the breaches that cost it a whole session;
# Sibling-B, Sibling-A and Sibling-D all track theirs. So do we.
#
# A negation cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so the
# exclusions below are on directory CONTENTS (`dir/*`) rather than on the
# directories themselves. Writing `.claude/` here instead would make the three
# negations that follow silently dead.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/commands/
.claude/commands/*
!.claude/commands/*.md
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/*.md
.mcp.json

# --- Editor / IDE -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Scratch ------------------------------------------------------------
_scratch/
tmp/
/commit_*.txt

# Cross-project correspondence channel. Notes are correspondence, not source -
# see moon_sync_inbox/README.md and ADR-004.
moon_sync_inbox/
